       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. PB231NATL.
      *> kb/Work PB231 - A BASED RECORD WITH A NATIONAL LEAF IS
      *> ORDINARY, CELL-BACKED STORAGE. IT RETIRES THE SECOND OF THE
      *> THREE BOUNDARIES conformance:negative/pb164-based-national-leaf
      *> PINNED (THE FIRST WAS THE USAGE BIT ONE,
      *> conformance:2002/pb231_based_bit_leaf; ONLY THE POINTER-CLASS
      *> LEAF IS LEFT), THE SAME WAY 2023/stepd_based_comp_leaf RETIRED
      *> pb151-based-comp-leaf: THE BIND-TIME COBOLNET1695 WAS
      *> REJECTING LEGAL COBOL.
      *> THE DERIVATION IS ONE-DIRECTIONAL AND USES NO ORACLE:
      *>   13.18.5.3 SR1/SR2 - THE ONLY RESTRICTIONS ON THE SUBJECT OF
      *>   A BASED ENTRY ARE "THE SUBJECT OF THE ENTRY SHALL NOT BE OF
      *>   CLASS OBJECT" AND "SHALL NOT BE A DYNAMIC-LENGTH ELEMENTARY
      *>   ITEM OR A VARIABLE-LENGTH GROUP". A GROUP WITH A NATIONAL
      *>   LEAF IS NEITHER (ITS CLASS IS NATIONAL, NOT OBJECT), AND NO
      *>   SYNTAX RULE ANYWHERE CONDITIONS BASED ON A SUBORDINATE'S
      *>   USAGE. 14.9.3.3 SR1 - ALLOCATE'S ONLY DEMAND ON data-name-1
      *>   IS "THE DATA ITEM REFERENCED BY data-name-1 SHALL BE
      *>   DESCRIBED WITH THE BASED CLAUSE".
      *> THE BYTE QUANTITY (14.9.3.4 GR3 - "THE AMOUNT OF STORAGE TO BE
      *> ALLOCATED IS THE NUMBER OF BYTES REQUIRED TO HOLD AN ITEM AS
      *> DESCRIBED BY data-name-1") IS A BYTE SUM, NOT A CHARACTER-
      *> POSITION SUM. 13.18.60.4 GR8 LEAVES THE NATIONAL SIZE TO THE
      *> IMPLEMENTOR - "NATIONAL CHARACTERS SHALL BE REPRESENTED IN THE
      *> STORAGE OF THE COMPUTER AS CHARACTERS OF A UNIFORM SIZE EQUAL
      *> TO OR A MULTIPLE OF THE SIZE OF CHARACTERS IN THE COMPUTER'S
      *> ALPHANUMERIC CHARACTER SET. EACH IMPLEMENTOR SHALL SPECIFY THE
      *> SIZE AND REPRESENTATION OF CHARACTERS STORED FOR USAGE
      *> NATIONAL" - AND COBOL.NET PINS TWO BYTES, UTF-16BE
      *> (DETERMINATION D-N1; CONFORMANCE.md ITEMS 33/188; THE SAME
      *> SERIALIZATION FUNCTION BYTE-LENGTH AND CONVERT'S RAW-STORAGE
      *> CHANNEL ALREADY ANSWER WITH). SO R IS LAID OUT:
      *>   R-N PIC N(3) -> BYTES 0-5 (THREE UTF-16BE PAIRS)
      *>   R-X PIC X(2) -> BYTES 6-7 (13.18.60.4 GR7, ONE BYTE EACH)
      *> GR3'S QUANTITY IS 8 BYTES, NOT THE 3+2 = 5 A CHARACTER-
      *> POSITION SUM WOULD GIVE. THE WINDOW RB PIC X(8) PROVES IT: A
      *> SHORTER CELL WOULD RAISE EC-BOUND-PTR AT THE DEREFERENCE
      *> (13.18.5.4 GR4), AND RB(8:1) READS THE LAST BYTE R OCCUPIES.
      *> GR4a AND GR4b ARE BOTH OBSERVED AND ARE OBSERVED TO BE THE
      *> SAME STORAGE: "a) IF THE RETURNING PHRASE IS SPECIFIED, THE
      *> DATA ITEM REFERENCED BY data-name-2 IS SET TO THE ADDRESS OF
      *> THAT STORAGE, b) IF data-name-1 IS SPECIFIED, THE ADDRESS OF
      *> THE BASED DATA ITEM REFERENCED BY data-name-1 IS SET TO THE
      *> ADDRESS OF THAT STORAGE" - R IS WRITTEN THROUGH ITS OWN
      *> IMPLICIT POINTER AND READ BACK THROUGH WS-P'S WINDOW.
      *> THE BYTES ARE READ WITH FUNCTION ORD, NEVER A SELF-INVERSE
      *> ROUND TRIP (15.70.1: "THE ORDINAL POSITION OF argument-1 IN
      *> THE PROGRAM COLLATING SEQUENCE. THE LOWEST ORDINAL POSITION IS
      *> 1", SO ORD IS THE BYTE VALUE + 1). N"ABC" IS U+0041 U+0042
      *> U+0043, SO THE PAIRS ARE 00 41 / 00 42 / 00 43 AND "YZ" IS
      *> 59 5A:
      *>   BYTE 0 = 0x00 =   0 -> ORD   1   (A, HIGH-ORDER FIRST)
      *>   BYTE 1 = 0x41 =  65 -> ORD  66   (A, LOW-ORDER)
      *>   BYTE 2 = 0x00 =   0 -> ORD   1   (B, HIGH-ORDER)
      *>   BYTE 3 = 0x42 =  66 -> ORD  67   (B, LOW-ORDER)
      *>   BYTE 6 = 0x59 =  89 -> ORD  90   ("Y")
      *>   BYTE 7 = 0x5A =  90 -> ORD  91   ("Z")
      *> THE HIGH-ORDER-FIRST ORDER IS ITSELF THE ASSERTION: A LITTLE-
      *> ENDIAN PAIR WOULD READ 66 1 67 1.
      *> THE BYTE->NATIONAL DIRECTION THEN PROVES THE CODEC IS AN
      *> INVOLUTION (THE R40 SIGN-LANE LESSON): BYTES WRITTEN THROUGH
      *> THE X VIEW WITH FUNCTION CHAR (15.15.1 - THE INVERSE OF ORD)
      *> READ BACK AS THE NATIONAL CHARACTER THEY ENCODE. CHAR(1) IS
      *> 0x00 AND CHAR(70) IS 0x45, SO PAIR 3 BECOMES U+0045 = "E" AND
      *> R-N READS "ABE".
      *> GR7 IS EXERCISED ON THE SECOND RECORD: "IF BOTH THE
      *> INITIALIZED PHRASE AND data-name-1 ARE SPECIFIED, THE
      *> ALLOCATED STORAGE IS INITIALIZED AS IF AN INITIALIZE
      *> data-name-1 WITH FILLER ALL TO VALUE THEN TO DEFAULT STATEMENT
      *> WERE EXECUTED". S-N CARRIES A VALUE AND TAKES IT (ALL TO
      *> VALUE); THE FILLER NATIONAL POSITION AND S-D DO NOT, SO THEY
      *> TAKE 14.9.20.4 GR6c's DEFAULT SENDING-OPERAND FOR THEIR
      *> CATEGORY - NATIONAL TAKES "FIGURATIVE CONSTANT NATIONAL
      *> SPACES", NUMERIC TAKES ZERO - AND WITH FILLER MEANS THE FILLER
      *> POSITION IS INCLUDED RATHER THAN SKIPPED. S IS 2*2 + 2*1 + 3 +
      *> 2 = 11 BYTES WHERE A CHARACTER-POSITION SUM SAYS 8, AND
      *> SB PIC X(11) READS ALL OF IT:
      *>   BYTE 0 = 0x00 -> ORD   1  ( "A" HIGH )
      *>   BYTE 1 = 0x41 -> ORD  66  ( "A" LOW  )
      *>   BYTE 4 = 0x00 -> ORD   1  ( FILLER NATIONAL SPACE, HIGH )
      *>   BYTE 5 = 0x20 -> ORD  33  ( FILLER NATIONAL SPACE, LOW  )
      *>   BYTE 6 = 0x30 -> ORD  49  ( S-D'S FIRST ZONED "0"       )
      *>   BYTE 10 = 0x49 -> ORD  74 ( "I" OF "HI" - THE LAST BYTE )
      *> WITHOUT "WITH FILLER" BYTES 4-5 WOULD HAVE BEEN LEFT AT THE
      *> UNDEFINED FILL.
      *> FREE TAKES THE POINTER, NOT THE RECORD (14.9.15.3 SR1).
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 R BASED.
          05 R-N PIC N(3).
          05 R-X PIC X(2).
       01 RB PIC X(8) BASED.
       01 S BASED.
          05 S-N   PIC N(2) VALUE N"AB".
          05 FILLER PIC N(1).
          05 S-D   PIC 9(3).
          05 S-X   PIC X(2) VALUE "HI".
       01 SB PIC X(11) BASED.
       01 WS-P USAGE POINTER.
       01 WS-Q USAGE POINTER.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
      *> GR4a + GR4b: ONE ALLOCATE, TWO ADDRESSES, ONE STORAGE.
           ALLOCATE R RETURNING WS-P
           SET ADDRESS OF RB TO WS-P
      *> Written through R's own implicit pointer (GR4b) ...
           MOVE N"ABC" TO R-N
           MOVE "YZ" TO R-X
           DISPLAY "N=[" R-N "] X=[" R-X "]"
      *> ... and read back through the RETURNING pointer's window (GR4a).
           DISPLAY "ORD=" FUNCTION ORD(RB(1:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(RB(2:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(RB(3:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(RB(4:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(RB(7:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(RB(8:1))
           DISPLAY "TAIL=[" RB(7:2) "]"
      *> The byte->national direction (the involution).
           MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(1) TO RB(5:1)
           MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(70) TO RB(6:1)
           DISPLAY "N=[" R-N "]"
           FREE WS-P
      *> GR7 over a record whose leaves include a national FILLER:
      *> ALL TO VALUE, THEN TO DEFAULT, WITH FILLER.
           ALLOCATE S INITIALIZED RETURNING WS-Q
           SET ADDRESS OF SB TO WS-Q
           DISPLAY "S-N=[" S-N "] S-D=" S-D " S-X=[" S-X "]"
           DISPLAY "SORD=" FUNCTION ORD(SB(1:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(SB(2:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(SB(5:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(SB(6:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(SB(7:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(SB(11:1))
           FREE WS-Q
           STOP RUN.
